  '2026-06-26T22:08:20.890452+00:00'::timestamptz,
  $$https://randomuser.me/api/portraits/women/87.jpg$$,
  $$https://picsum.photos/seed/amara-diallo/800/200$$,
  $$Amara Diallo brings nine years of hands-on experience in monitoring, evaluation, and learning across East and West Africa. She has led the design of results frameworks, performance monitoring plans, and impact evaluations for major donors including USAID, FCDO, and UN Women. Her work consistently integrates gender and social inclusion lenses, ensuring that data collection tools capture disaggregated evidence and that program learning reaches marginalized populations. Amara is fluent in Swahili and French, which has enabled her to work effectively with government counterparts and community-based organizations across Francophone and Anglophone contexts. She holds an MSc in Development Economics from the University of London and is a certified MEAL practitioner. She also designs results frameworks for new programmes and has a growing practice in youth employment and women's economic empowerment.$$,
  $$[{"name":"Gender Mainstreaming","tier":"core"},{"name":"Gender-Based Violence","tier":"core"},{"name":"Monitoring & Evaluation","tier":"core"},{"name":"Qualitative Research","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Survey Design","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Statistical Analysis","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Program Design & Proposal Writing","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Youth Development","tier":"strong"},{"name":"Women's Economic Empowerment","tier":"working"},{"name":"Evidence Synthesis","tier":"working"}]$$::jsonb,
