  $$James Okafor is an emerging specialist in geospatial analysis and climate data, with a focus on applying satellite remote sensing and open-source GIS tools to environmental and development challenges in sub-Saharan Africa. Over four years, he has mapped coastal erosion, deforestation fronts, and urban heat islands for programs funded by UNDP and NASA's SERVIR initiative. He is proficient in QGIS, ArcGIS, Google Earth Engine, and Python-based spatial analysis, and has built web-based mapping dashboards for non-technical government audiences. James is passionate about open data and participatory mapping approaches that put spatial intelligence directly in the hands of local communities. He holds a BSc in Geomatics from the University of Lagos. He also builds flood and drought early warning layers for national hydromet services and monitors forest loss for land-use planning.$$,
