  $$Fatmata Kamara is an agricultural research officer with four years of experience on sustainable farming and food security in Sierra Leone. She has coordinated farmer field school surveys on rice and cassava, mapped plot boundaries with GPS and QGIS for a land-use study, and supported the evaluation of an inland valley swamp rehabilitation project. She designs short survey questionnaires on tablets, trains enumerators, and writes field reports for district agricultural offices. Fatmata is interested in agroecology and climate-smart practices that reduce slash-and-burn clearing on upland farms. She also prepares extension messages from on-farm trials and has mapped customary land claims for farmer groups.$$,
