  $$Hervé Nkeng Tabi is a biodiversity and forest mapping specialist with ten years of experience in Cameroon and the Congo Basin. He produces GIS maps of forest cover, community forests and wildlife corridors, and has supported participatory mapping with Baka and Bagyeli Indigenous Peoples to document customary land use. His work has fed into protected area management plans, deforestation-free cocoa supply chain studies and sustainable farming projects around forest edges. Hervé facilitates village meetings in French and English and trains forest guards and NGO staff in GPS data collection. He also supports environmental and social safeguards work, especially free, prior and informed consent with forest communities.$$,
