  $$https://picsum.photos/seed/demo-lerato-mokoena/800/200$$,
  $$Lerato Mokoena is a social protection policy analyst with sixteen years of experience in South Africa and the SADC region. She models the cost and poverty impact of social grants with tax-benefit microsimulation, has evaluated disability grant assessment processes, and advises treasury and social development officials on reform options. Her statistical analysis work in R and Stata draws on household and labour force surveys, and she writes for both technical and political audiences. Lerato has worked with the National Treasury, UNICEF and the ILO, and has a particular interest in disability inclusion in social protection systems. She has also tested behavioural nudges to raise grant take-up and works on economic inclusion programmes for grant recipients.$$,
